      <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
      
      <h3>1.1 Personal Information Provided Directly by You</h3>
      <p>When you browse our Site, create an account, initiate an order, or communicate with our support team, we collect personal data necessary to execute transactions and deliver customer service:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Identity & Demographic Data:</strong> First name, last name, username, government ID details if requested for high-value fraud verification.</li>
        <li><strong>Contact Information:</strong> Billing address, shipping address, email address, and telephone number.</li>
        <li><strong>Financial & Payment Data:</strong> Credit card, debit card, or alternative payment details. Payment data is processed directly via PCI-DSS compliant gateways (Shopify Payments, PayPal). We never store raw credit card numbers on our local servers.</li>
        <li><strong>Transaction History:</strong> Records of products ordered, order dates, payment status, shipping tracking codes, warranty claims, and return requests.</li>
        <li><strong>Communications Data:</strong> Transcripts of emails, contact form submissions, order notes, and reviews submitted to us.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>1.2 Automatically Collected Technical Data</h3>
      <p>As you navigate bikebee.shop, our hosting infrastructure and analytical tools automatically log standard web usage parameters:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Device & Network Data:</strong> Internet Protocol (IP) address, browser version and configuration, operating system, device screen resolution, and time zone.</li>
        <li><strong>Browsing & Engagement Data:</strong> Pages viewed, dwell time, navigation paths, referring URLs, search terms utilized within our store, and page load times.</li>
        <li><strong>Location Data:</strong> Approximate geographic location (city, state, country) derived from your IP address to estimate applicable shipping times and tax rates.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>1.3 Data from Trusted Third Parties</h3>
      <p>We receive supplementary verification data from authenticated partners, including:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Shopify Inc.:</strong> Our hosting and storefront engine.</li>
        <li><strong>Payment Processors:</strong> Shopify Payments, PayPal, Shop Pay (fraud risk scoring, payment capture confirmation).</li>
        <li><strong>Logistics Providers:</strong> FedEx, UPS, and USPS (delivery timestamps, recipient signatures, transit milestones).</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics Partners:</strong> Google Analytics (aggregated site performance metrics).</li>
      </ul>
