    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>6. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
      
      <h3>6.1 California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA / CPRA) Rights</h3>
      <p>If you are a California resident, California Civil Code Section 1798.100 et seq. grants you specific rights concerning your personal information:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Right to Know / Access:</strong> You may request disclosure of the specific pieces and categories of personal information we have collected, the sources, commercial purposes, and categories of third parties with whom it was shared over the past 12 months.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Deletion:</strong> You may request deletion of personal information we have collected from you, subject to statutory exemptions (such as completing an ongoing order, warranty servicing, or legal tax compliance).</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Correct Inaccurate Information:</strong> You may request correction of inaccurate personal data maintained in our records.</li>
        <li><strong>Right to Non-Discrimination:</strong> We will never deny services, charge different prices, or provide a differing quality of service if you choose to exercise any of your statutory CCPA rights.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise your California privacy rights, please email us at <a href="mailto:contact@bikebee.shop">contact@bikebee.shop</a> with the subject line <strong>"CCPA Privacy Request"</strong> and specify your full name, shipping address, and order reference.</p>

      <h3>6.2 European Union & UK Residents (GDPR Rights)</h3>
      <p>Under GDPR Articles 15–22, EEA and UK individuals possess the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict processing of, object to the processing of, and request portability of their personal data. Submit requests to <a href="mailto:contact@bikebee.shop">contact@bikebee.shop</a>.</p>
    </section>

